---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE_DATA } from '../constants';
import portraitImage from '../assets/portrait.png';

import '../styles/about.css';
---

<Layout pageTitle="About">
    <div class="page-container">
        <h1>About Me</h1>

        <div class="about-content">
            <div class="about-intro-wrapper centered-column">
                <div class="about-header centered-column">
                    <Image src={portraitImage} alt={SITE_DATA.name} class="about-portrait" />
                    <h2 class="about-name">{SITE_DATA.name}</h2>
                </div>

                <p class="intro-text">
                    For over twenty years, I have helped NYC’s top students transform academic stress into confidence and high achievement. Since 2003, I have worked full-time as an educator in New York City, balancing a dedicated private tutoring practice with my current role as a local high school teacher. I have guided students through the rigorous curriculums of the city's most competitive institutions. My track record includes helping high schoolers excel at elite academies like Horace Mann, Bronx Science, and Trinity, as well as mentoring undergraduates navigating demanding pre-med tracks at Columbia and NYU. Whether a student is tackling advanced high school coursework or high-stakes university STEM classes, my approach is deeply patient, highly encouraging, and entirely tailored to how they learn.
                <br><br>
                    I tutor a broad spectrum of math and science subjects because I love the variety—and that multi-subject fluency is a massive advantage for my students. Education shouldn't feel fragmented. When a student and I build great rapport and a strong working rhythm in physics, they don't have to hunt for a new tutor when chemistry or calculus rolls around next semester. I provide a consistent, reliable academic partnership that adapts as your student's workload evolves. Based in Manhattan, I am proud to offer focused, in-person tutoring for local families as well as flexible Zoom sessions for students anywhere.                
                <br><br>
                     Curious about what our sessions will actually be like? You can <strong><a href="/videos">watch a sample video in which I talk about prime numbers</a></strong> to experience my teaching style and see exactly what a student sees on their screen during a lesson.
                </p>
            </div>

            <section>
                <h2>Subjects Covered</h2>
                <ul class="education-list icon-list">
                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">High School</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">From Honors Physics and advanced tracks to AP Physics 1, 2, and C (Mechanics & E&M), I help students at elite NYC independent and prep schools like Trinity, Dalton, Horace Mann, and Chapin master the coursework, and I have a strong, proven track record of helping them secure a 5 on the exam.</span>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">College & University</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">For undergraduates and post-bacs tackling first-year General Physics I and II—whether algebra or calculus-based—I specialize in helping pre-med students at NYU, Columbia, and other institutions master their foundational science requirements, protect their GPA, and stay on target for medical school and related competitive paths.</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>


            <section>
                <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                <ul class="custom-list">
                   <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">Do you provide worksheets or study guides?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">Yes. I've accumulated a vast array of textbooks and problem sets. I'll often provide my students with problem sets so they can continue building their skills after our session is over. I also frequently make electronic flash cards for students who are studying a memorization-intensive course.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">How long is an average session?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">An hour and a half is a typical session length. I ask that sessions be a minimum of an hour long.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">Do you assign homework?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">Yes, if it is needed.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">Can I share my session with another student?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">Sure! Ask me about my special rates for group sessions.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">Do you tutor in person on online?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">I do much of my tutoring on Zoom. I'm located in NYC, so I'm available to in-person sessions.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">What happens if I have to cancel? Do I still have to pay for the session?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">I require 24 hours of notice for cancellations, or I will expect you to pay for the session you missed.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">What forms of payment do you accept?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">Cash, Venmo, PayPal, and Zelle.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">Do you offer any referral bonuses?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">Yes. If you recommend me to another student, and that student hires me for four hours or more, you get one hour of free tutoring.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">What is a typical session like for high school and college tutoring on academic subjects?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">For academic subjects, my students are usually already enrolled in a course in high school or college. Usually we go over homework together, I teach them new information as it is needed to answer the questions, and try to guide them through their homework without directly answering the question for them. This helps my students increase their problem solving ability. I can also lecture if needed, make up problems for practice, and assign problems additional practice on their own time. Oftentimes I will create reference sheets for my students as I tutor them, and sometimes I have reference sheets already prepared. Usually we'll meet for an hour and a half.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">What is a typical session like for test prep?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">Test prep tutoring is different, because usually it is not in conjunction with another class, so I'll spend more time lecturing and explaining concepts, and then we'll go over problems together, and I'll assign homework that we can go over at the next session.</span>
                    </li>

                    <li>
                        <span class="list-item-title">How can you be contacted?</span>
                        <span class="list-item-description">HIOAHOIHIOHOOIH</span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>


            <section>
                <h2>Contact</h2>
                <p>
                    If you have any questions or if you'd like to schedule an appointment, you can email me at
                    <a href={`mailto:${SITE_DATA.email}`}>cjhellwig@gmail.com</a>, or text or call me at 718-753-7060.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>
</Layout>
